WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.393
The lasting takeaway is that the right problem
formulation changes what is tractable.

00:00:05.473 --> 00:00:12.090
By expressing rematerialization decisions as a
small set of retention intervals in a constraint program,

00:00:12.170 --> 00:00:18.078
Moccasin reduces the number of discrete variables
from quadratic to linear in the graph size.

00:00:18.158 --> 00:00:24.131
That single change lets it scale to compute graphs
far larger than prior methods could handle,

00:00:24.211 --> 00:00:30.312
solving them up to ten times faster while keeping
the added runtime overhead under five percent.

00:00:30.392 --> 00:00:33.725
And because the output is just an execution sequence,

00:00:33.805 --> 00:00:36.880
the resulting schedule can run on any CPU or GPU.
